Dear Dr. Dieujuste,

I hope you are doing well.

As a follow-up to our recent conversations, I am pleased to share several
materials from Renaissance Group for your review ahead of our meeting
tomorrow, including the Scope of Services, the concept narrative addressing
postpartum depression and maternal wellness, and the proposed agenda for
our discussion.

The materials have been developed based on our conversations and the vision
you have shared for creating an organization focused on improving
postpartum maternal health, with particular attention to the experiences
and needs of Black and Haitian immigrant mothers and families. We believe
there is an important opportunity to develop a culturally responsive
organization that addresses not only postpartum depression, but also the
isolation, lack of support, cultural barriers, and gaps in access to
appropriate maternal and mental-health resources that many women and
families experience.

We would especially appreciate your review of the concept narrative. Our
intention with this document is to begin putting structure around the
broader vision you have described and to articulate the need, the
population being served, the potential programs, and the long-term vision
for the organization. We view this as a working concept that can continue
to evolve based on your expertise, research, clinical perspective, and the
specific outcomes you ultimately want the organization to achieve.

Your professional experience, doctoral research, understanding of the lived
experiences of Haitian immigrant women, and knowledge of maternal and
behavioral health provide a strong foundation for this initiative.
Renaissance Group's role would be to help translate that expertise into a
clearly defined organizational model with the infrastructure, programs,
partnerships, funding strategy, and positioning necessary to become a
sustainable nonprofit.

The Scope of Services outlines the areas in which Renaissance Group can
support that development. This includes organizational and strategic
development, governance and board development, program design, business and
operational planning, proposal development and fundraising strategy,
community outreach and communications, evaluation and measurable outcomes,
strategic partnerships, and the development of the organizational materials
necessary to position the organization effectively with funders and
external stakeholders.

A key focus will be ensuring that the organization's programs are clearly
defined and connected to measurable community outcomes. We want to
establish a framework that allows your research and professional expertise
to remain at the center of the organization while creating programs that
can be communicated effectively to funders, healthcare institutions,
universities, community organizations, maternal-health providers,
mental-health professionals, and other strategic partners.

We also believe that partnerships will be particularly important to the
organization's long-term success. Relationships with hospitals, health
centers, doulas, maternal-health providers, behavioral-health
professionals, universities, faith-based organizations, immigrant-serving
organizations, and other community-based partners can create a broader
support network around mothers and families and significantly expand the
organization's ability to reach those who may otherwise remain underserved.

The ultimate objective is not simply to establish another nonprofit, but to
build an organization with a clear mission, strong governance, well-defined
programs, measurable impact, meaningful community partnerships, and a
sustainable funding model. Over time, the organization should be positioned
not only to provide direct support, but also to become a credible voice and
resource within the broader maternal-health and postpartum wellness
landscape.

For tomorrow's meeting, we have also included a proposed agenda to help
guide the conversation. The goal is to use our time to review the overall
concept, discuss the priorities you believe should be at the center of the
organization, review the proposed programs and strategic direction, discuss
the Scope of Services, and identify the immediate next steps required to
begin moving the vision from concept into implementation.

Please take some time to review the attached materials before our
discussion. We welcome your comments, questions, additions, and
recommendations. In particular, your feedback on the concept narrative will
be valuable in ensuring that the organization's direction accurately
reflects your research, experience, and vision.

The documents are intended to provide a strong starting framework rather
than a finished product. We expect that the strategy, programs, and
organizational structure will continue to be refined through our
discussions and as we further define the organization's priorities.

We appreciate the opportunity to work with you on this initiative. We
believe there is significant potential to build something meaningful and
sustainable around the foundation you have already established, and we look
forward to exploring that opportunity with you.

I look forward to our discussion tomorrow.

Best regards,

Paris Swindle
Chairman
Renaissance Group
